## 4. Summary of the fix

| Failure mode | Fix |
|---|---|
| Erasures ignored / wrong BW ansatz | Build `g(x)=∏(x-x_i)`, seek `Q = f·g·Λ` with `Λ` monic |
| Divide-by-zero in elimination | Gaussian elimination **with column pivoting** and free-column handling |
| Wrong solvability / unknown count | `k + 2t + e` unknowns vs `n` equations; correct bound `2t+e<=n-k` |
| Nontrivial divisions always fail | Correct `polyDivMod` shift `i-d+j` (was `i-j`) |
| Silent miscorrection | Independent re-encoding verifier requires `agree >= n - t - e` |
| Too few errors but fixed `t=tMax` | Monic-`Λ` system stays consistent; any solution yields `f = Q/(gΛ)` |
| Too many errors | Inconsistent system or failed verification ⇒ explicit `{success:false}` |

The implementation is directly usable: paste `rs.js`, choose `new rs.GF(8, 0x11d)` or `new rs.GF(16, 0x1002d)`, and call `rs.decode(gf, n, k, xs, ys, erasures)`. It returns `{success, message, corrected, t, e, agree}` on success and `{success:false, reason}` otherwise.
